From 56115b5b3fca4632cae888e3f64803c0d78589ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?A=CC=82nderson=20Q?= <anquadros@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 17:16:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] terminal: Add activity-driven terminal theme switching

Switch each terminal's theme automatically by activity state: one theme
while a command runs, another while idle at the shell prompt. Configured
via the new "terminal.activity_theme": { "busy", "idle" } setting; unset
by default (no behavior change).

Activity is a heuristic (Zed does not parse OSC 133 prompt markers): the
terminal is busy while a running task is active, or while its foreground
process is something other than a known shell. Because foreground-process
info is otherwise only refreshed on terminal output, a lightweight poll
runs while the feature is enabled so silent commands (e.g. sleep) still
register. Both transitions are debounced so fast or back-to-back commands
do not strobe the theme.

Builds on per-terminal theme overrides: activity drives the same override
a user sets by hand, and an explicit "theme: terminal" choice suppresses
activity switching for that terminal until cleared.
