From: =?UTF-8?q?A=CC=82nderson=20Q?= <anquadros@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 21:44:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] terminal: Add activity theme toggle and output-based
 interactive detection

Add a "terminal: toggle activity theme" action that turns activity
switching on and off via an "enabled" flag in terminal.activity_theme,
keeping the configured busy/idle theme names across toggles.

Refine detection for interactive foreground programs (editors, pagers,
REPLs, and other long-running prompts). Such a program holds the
terminal foreground the whole time it is open, so presence alone no
longer means busy: it is busy only while it is actively producing output
and idle once that output stops. One-shot commands are unchanged. The
built-in interactive set is extensible via an "interactive_programs"
setting.
